bg3le Ext.UI: optionally serialize Ext.UI calls with View::Update (off by default)

On top of 0001. Closes the window 0001 leaves: between Lua reading a child pointer and
AddReference(), the UI thread could free the child. With BG3LE_UI_SERIALIZE=1 in the
environment, or Ext._Internal.UiSerialize(true) at run time, each Ext.UI C function runs
under a recursive timed mutex that the View::Update hooks hold for the frame. Lua waits at
most 50 ms (the UI thread may itself be waiting on the client Lua lock inside a routed event
handler), then runs unserialized; UiSerialize() returns (on, timeouts).
Lua is compiled as C++, so a Lua error unwinds through the lock guard.
---
